    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0694" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4483: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-27T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 27—11:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>423. Following telegram has been sent American consul general at Canton: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 27, 3 p.m. Your December 21, 3 p.m.<anchor n="91"
                                xml:id="d437-f1"/> I understand Aglen has replied through
                            commissioner of customs to Wu. I have not seen text but understand he
                            refers to various international agreements and explains why it is
                            impossible for him to comply with request but lets Sun down as easily as
                            possible.</p>
                        <p>Your despatches 37, 38 and 40 received today.<anchor n="92"
                                xml:id="d437-f2"/> Your conduct of this delicate and difficult
                            affair very gratifying to the Legation. It is absolutely essential that
                            solidarity of foreign powers should be preserved. “Who becomes senior
                            consul on Jamieson’s departure?”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
